E-commerce sales pipeline
End-to-end processing for the sales exports (customers, products, orders) that land in data/ next to this notebook.

The flow is the usual layered thing:

Raw - each source file lands as its own table; values untouched except for a blank-row guard, headers snake_cased (delta won't take spaces)
Enriched - cleaned customers and products, plus a fact table joining orders to both (profit rounded to 2dp)
Aggregate - profit rolled up by year x category x sub-category x customer
SQL cuts on top of the aggregate for the stakeholders
Quirks worth knowing about (found the hard way while exploring the files):

order dates in the json are day-first - 21/8/2016 is Aug 21, and parsing them the other way silently lands everything in the wrong month
the customer sheet's used range is bigger than the actual data, so trailing blank rows need filtering
a few product ids in the orders have no entry in the product master (~200 rows) - those get category Unknown instead of being dropped
customer names have digits and punctuation jammed into them (Gary567 Hansen), we strip the junk but can't reconstruct what was corrupted
a few dozen product names contain inch marks (") in unquoted csv fields, which shifts those rows over by one during parsing - the enriched products cell shifts what it can back and flags the rows, the price is lost in the parse
a few customers have no name at all in the source sheet - they keep their id and country in the fact table, the name lands as Unknown
Run top to bottom. Tests live in ecommerce_sales_tests.

