4. Aggregate table
Profit at the finest grain anyone asked for: year x product category x product sub-category x customer. Every other cut (year only, customer only, year + category, customer + year) is just a rollup of this table, which is exactly how the SQL in the next section uses it.

agg_profit_by_year_category_subcategory_customer = (
    enriched_orders
    .groupBy("order_year", "category", "sub_category", "customer_id", "customer_name")
    .agg(
        F.round(F.sum("profit"), 2).alias("total_profit"),
        F.countDistinct("order_id").alias("order_count"),
        F.sum("quantity").alias("units_sold"),
    )
)

(
    agg_profit_by_year_category_subcategory_customer.write
    .mode("overwrite")
    .saveAsTable(f"{SCHEMA}.agg_profit_by_year_category_subcategory_customer")
)

print(f"aggregate rows: {agg_profit_by_year_category_subcategory_customer.count()}")

